    "description": "The Surrey Pretrial Services Centre Expansion Project is a correctional infrastructure PPP in British Columbia. Its end user is the provincial justice and corrections system, with economics characteristic of long-term public-sector infrastructure contracts. The project is asset-heavy and availability-based rather than demand-risk exposed. Public sources describe the scope as a 216-cell expansion together with renovations to the existing facility. Current project-level revenue and ownership percentages were not publicly disclosed in the reviewed materials. The asset is associated with Jura Acquisition, the vehicle backed by funds managed by Equitix and Dalmore following the 2018 take-private of John Laing Infrastructure Fund.",
